# Loaded by `npm run dev:live` — the real Spring Boot API, NO MOCKS AT ALL.
#
# VITE_ENABLE_MOCK_API=false switches the worker off entirely, so VITE_LIVE_API is not
# consulted in this mode and nothing falls back to a fixture. Read that before using this
# file: it is all-or-nothing, and `npm run dev` with VITE_LIVE_API is the setting that
# mixes the two.
#
# WHAT YOU WILL SEE, and why it is not a fault in the front end.
#
# The backend implements registration (personal only), sign-in, the session and the staff
# portal. Everything else — accounts, transactions, cards, loans, notifications, transfers,
# payments, statements — has no controller yet.
#
# Those do NOT come back 401. A signed-in customer holds ROLE_CUSTOMER, so the catch-all
# in SecurityConfig GRANTS the request; Spring then finds no handler and returns 404. The
# dashboard renders that as "we could not find that, so it may have been removed or it may
# not be yours to view" on every panel, which looks like a broken portal and is really an
# unbuilt one. (An earlier version of this comment said "everything else will 401", which
# was true when only /health existed and sent a debugging session down the wrong path.)
#
# So use `npm run dev` for walking the onboarding flow. Use this mode only when you
# specifically want no mock worker running at all.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/v1
VITE_API_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
VITE_APP_VERSION=0.1.0-dev
VITE_ENABLE_MOCK_API=false
